+# Windows ARM64 Port
+
+Native Windows ARM64 support for util-linux 2.40.2, the version in the MSYS2 (`usr/bin`) layer of Git for Windows, on branch `arm64-port`. The target is the MSYS/Cygwin POSIX layer: host triplet `aarch64-pc-cygwin`, linked against the ARM64 `msys-2.0.dll`. MSVC cannot build this code. The compiler is the `aarch64-pc-cygwin` cross GCC 17, and MSVC's `dumpbin` is used only to check the binaries.
+
+## Summary of Changes
+### Build System
+- `configure.ac`, `configure`: one line each, `LIBS="$LTLIBINTL"` instead of `LIBS="$LIBINTL"` (commit `03a6252`).
+  - In the cross build, gettext's lib-link macros resolve libintl to an absolute `.../libintl.dll.a`.
+  - When libtool links a shared library, it treats an absolute `*.a` argument as a static archive. With Cygwin's `file_magic` method it then drops that archive, so `libblkid.la` failed with an undefined `libintl_gettext`.
+  - `LTLIBINTL` (`-L<dir> -lintl`) is the libtool form of the same flags and is what `Makefile.am` already uses. Native builds are unchanged.
+  - This replaces the `lt_cv_deplibs_check_method=pass_all` override in the MSYS2 recipe. That override's comment ("libtool only recognises x86 import libraries") has the wrong cause: `func_win32_libid` already matches `pe-aarch64`.
+- `config/config.guess`: adds an `aarch64:CYGWIN*:*:*` case, so `configure` without `--build` works on a native ARM64 Cygwin host (commit `100ca63`). Upstream config.guess has had this case since 2023.
+### Source Code
+None. The only x86 code in the built sources is in `include/xxhash.h`, and it is fully guarded. util-linux defines `XXH_NO_XXH3`, so only the scalar XXH32/XXH64 code is compiled. With XXH3 enabled, the header would pick `XXH_NEON` on aarch64 GCC. The x86 code in `lscpu`, `setarch` and `audit-arch.h` is Linux-only and is not built on Cygwin.
+### CI/CD
+None (the release tree has no CI).
+### New Files
+- `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.txt`, `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.meta.json`: baseline benchmark results (commit `0b98b5f`).
+
+## Build Steps (ARM64)
+Prerequisites:
+- x86_64 MSYS2 at `C:\msys64` with the `aarch64-pc-cygwin` cross toolchain (binutils 2.47.50, GCC 17).
+- An ARM64 sysroot in `/usr/aarch64-pc-cygwin` containing msys2-runtime, gettext, libiconv, readline, ncurses, sqlite, libxcrypt and zlib. All of these were checked as `AA64`.
+- `crossarm64/config.site` from the MSYS2-packages aarch64 branch.
+
+### Build
+```bash
+MSYSTEM=MSYS /c/msys64/usr/bin/bash -lc '
+export CONFIG_SITE=/home/HCKTest/MSYS2-packages/crossarm64/config.site MSYSTEM=CYGWIN PATH="$PATH:/usr/aarch64-pc-cygwin/usr/bin"
+export OBJDUMP=aarch64-pc-cygwin-objdump NM=aarch64-pc-cygwin-nm AR=aarch64-pc-cygwin-ar RANLIB=aarch64-pc-cygwin-ranlib \
+       STRIP=aarch64-pc-cygwin-strip DLLTOOL=aarch64-pc-cygwin-dlltool CC=aarch64-pc-cygwin-gcc
+export CFLAGS="-O2 -pipe --param=ggc-min-heapsize=2000000 --param=ggc-min-expand=1000" CPPFLAGS="-D__USE_LINUX_IOCTL_DEFS"
+mkdir -p /c/wos-eval/work/util-linux/build-arm64 && cd /c/wos-eval/work/util-linux/build-arm64
+../configure --build=x86_64-pc-cygwin --host=aarch64-pc-cygwin <option list from the MSYS2 util-linux PKGBUILD build()> SOLIB_LDFLAGS=-no-undefined
+make -j8
+make DESTDIR=$PWD/dest install'
+```
+- The full command is in `build-arm64/build.sh`.
+- The `--param=ggc-*` flags work around a garbage-collector hang/ICE in the cross `cc1`.
+- Build output: `build-arm64/dest/usr/bin`, containing 50 `.exe` and 5 `.dll` files.
+
+### Run Tests
+- Cross-build the helpers with `make -C build-arm64 -j8 check-programs`.
+- From an ARM64 MSYS userland, run `tests/run.sh --builddir=<build-arm64> --parallel=8` with `PATH=<build-arm64>/.libs:/usr/bin` and `SHELL=/usr/bin/bash` (the ARM64 bash must not inherit an x64 `SHELL`).
+
+Expected: 84 OK, 10 failed, 2 known-fail, 217 skipped. Every failure also occurs on x86_64 (see below).
+
+### Run Benchmarks
+```bash
+bash util-linux-scratch/bench/gen-data.sh
+bash util-linux-scratch/bench/run-all.sh
+```
+The results are written to `benchmarks/base_bench_win_arm.txt`.
+
+## Test Results
+- **Build host**: native ARM64 (Snapdragon X Elite). The cross compiler runs under x64 emulation; the tests run natively.
+- **Executed**: yes, 313 test scripts.
+- **Results**:
+
+| Run | OK | Failed | Known-fail | Skipped | Timeout | Subtests OK/failed |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| ARM64 | 84 | 10 | 2 | 217 | 0 | 586 / 21 |
+| x86_64 build of the same tree | 84 | 10 | 2 | 217 | 0 | 586 / 21 |
+
+Every failure is the same on x86_64, with byte-identical diffs, so they all come from Cygwin/MSYS rather than the port:
+- `getopt/options` (7 subtests): Cygwin getopt's error message wording.
+- `col/multibyte`, `misc/mbsencode`: printability of UTF-8 bytes in the POSIX locale.
+- `hardlink/options`: `noacl` modes.
+- `rename/symlink`, `rename/subdir`: MSYS symlink emulation.
+- `script/*`: Cygwin pty.
+- `liblastlog2/dlopen`: the test expects a `.so`.
+- `liblastlog2/write_read_user`, `liblastlog2/y2038_ll2_read_all`: sqlite open.
+
+The skips are tests that need root (45) or tools that are Linux-only or disabled in configure.
+
+## Test Fixes Applied
+None. There were no ARM64-specific failures.
+
