+## NEON Optimizations
+Phase 7 was skipped because `WOS_SKIP_OPTIMIZE` was set. The built code has no x86 SIMD paths to replace.
+
+## ARM64 vs x64 Performance Comparison
+No x64 benchmark reference was supplied, so the differential comparison does not apply. The baseline table above includes x64-under-emulation numbers for context.
+
+## Architecture Verification
+`dumpbin /HEADERS` (MSVC 14.51, HostARM64) reports `AA64 machine (ARM64)` for all 55 of the 55 installed binaries, including `getopt.exe`, `column.exe`, `msys-uuid-1.dll`, `msys-smartcols-1.dll`, `msys-blkid-1.dll` and `msys-fdisk-1.dll`. The 131 `test_*`/`sample-*` helper programs are AA64 as well.
+
+## Arm AppReady Status
+- **Target profile**: native ARM64 (aarch64-pc-cygwin).
+- **Stages reached**: Assess, Build, Deploy (the binaries ran natively), Optimize skipped.
+- **Dependencies**: msys2-runtime, gettext, libiconv, readline, ncurses, sqlite, libxcrypt, zlib and gcc-libs are all cross-built ARM64 MSYS2 packages and checked as AA64. The WoA dashboard does not track the MSYS ABI.
+- **App Assure escalation**: none needed.
+
+## Limitations & Known Issues
+- [hard-external] The 45 root-only tests can never run on Cygwin/MSYS. `ts_skip_nonroot` requires `$UID == 0`, and there is no uid 0 on Cygwin: even an elevated administrator shell reports `id -u` = 197608.
+- The performance gap on stream workloads is a residual, not a defect. On hexdump, rev and column, ARM64 is 10-24% slower than the x64 build of the same tree under emulation. Process-spawn-bound workloads are 1.7-1.9x faster. The stream gap has not been profiled. It is plausibly in the ARM64 `msys-2.0.dll` stdio path, which is outside this repository.
+
+## Reverting / Coexistence
+The x86_64 build is unchanged; the `LTLIBINTL` form is what native builds already resolve to. To build x86_64, configure without `--host`.
